error BYN1032: `if !x {…}` with no `else` is an input form; write `unless x {…}`

  3 │     if (!x) {
    │     ^^^^^^^ a negated condition with no `else`
    │
  help: write `unless` with the condition as written
    │ 3 │     unless x {
    │   │     ++++++++

error BYN1007: `unless` with a negated condition is a double negative

  6 │     unless (!x) print("b");
    │     ^^^^^^^^^^^ `unless` already negates
    │
  help: use `if` with the condition as written
    │ 6 │     if x print("b");
    │   │     ++++

error BYN1018: the body of `unless` must be a block

  6 │     unless (!x) print("b");
    │                 ^^^^^^^^^^ a single statement
    │
  help: wrap the statement in `{ }`
    │ 6 │     unless (!x) { print("b"); }
    │   │                 +++++++++++++++

error BYN1022: `unless` with `&&`/`||` reads as a double negative

  7 │     unless (x && x) print("c");
    │     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ a compound condition
    │
  help: use `if` with the negated condition
    │ 7 │     if !(x && x) print("c");
    │   │     ++++

error BYN1018: the body of `unless` must be a block

  7 │     unless (x && x) print("c");
    │                     ^^^^^^^^^^ a single statement
    │
  help: wrap the statement in `{ }`
    │ 7 │     unless (x && x) { print("c"); }
    │   │                     +++++++++++++++

error BYN1017: parentheses around a condition are an input form

  8 │     if (!x) {
    │        ^^^^ not needed
    │
  help: remove the parentheses
    │ 8 │     if !x {
    │   │        ++
